      "proposition": {
        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<ul><li><p>Woods pleads no contest to reduced charge</p></li><li><p>Charges stemmed from March rollover crash</p></li></ul><p>Tiger Woods pleaded no contest to reckless driving on Wednesday morning as part of an agreement with Florida prosecutors that reduced a DUI charge stemming <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/mar/27/tiger-woods-rollover-crash-florida-jupiter-island\">from his rollover crash in March</a>.</p><p>The 50-year-old was adjudicated guilty of willful and wanton reckless driving, a second offense, during a hearing in Martin County court. Under the agreement, Woods was fined $1,000 and had his driver’s license suspended for five years. Prosecutors had originally charged him with driving under the influence with property damage.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/sep/02/tiger-woods-change-plea-dui-florida-crash\">Continue reading...</a>"
